@{
}

<div class="columns">
    <div class="column is-8">
        <div class="content">
            <h2 class="is-size-6">Advanced settings</h2>
            <p>These settings are typically administred by the RP but for demo purposes we expose them to you for testing behaviours and browser support</p>
            <form id="options">
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Attestation type</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-attestation">
                                <option value="none">None</option>
                                <option value="indirect">Indirect</option>
                                <option selected value="direct">Direct</option>
                                <option value="enterprise">Enterprise</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Authenticator</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-authenticator">
                                <option value="">Not specified</option>
                                <option selected value="cross-platform">Cross Platform (Token)</option>
                                <option value="platform">Platform (TPM)</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">User verification</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-userverification">
                                <option value="required">Required</option>
                                <option selected value="preferred">Preferred</option>
                                <option value="discouraged">Discouraged</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">UserVerification can be changed for both register & login</p>

                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Resident Key</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-residentkey">
                                <option value="required">Required</option>
                                <option selected value="preferred">Preferred</option>
                                <option value="discouraged">Discouraged</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">For register the client will guide the user through setting up user verification if needed to create a discoverable credential. This takes precedence over the setting of userVerification.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="label">Algorithms (pubKeyCredParams)</label>
                    <div class="control">
                        <div class="select">
                            <select id="option-algorithms">
                                <option selected value="">Server default (ML-DSA-87, ML-DSA-65, ML-DSA-44, ES256, RS256, EdDSA)</option>
                                <option value="-50,-49,-48">PQC only (ML-DSA-87, ML-DSA-65, ML-DSA-44)</option>
                                <option value="-50">ML-DSA-87 only (-50)</option>
                                <option value="-49">ML-DSA-65 only (-49)</option>
                                <option value="-48">ML-DSA-44 only (-48)</option>
                                <option value="-7,-257,-8">Classical only (ES256, RS256, EdDSA)</option>
                                <option value="-7">ES256 only (-7)</option>
                                <option value="-35">ES384 only (-35)</option>
                                <option value="-257">RS256 only (-257)</option>
                                <option value="-8">EdDSA / Ed25519 only (-8)</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="help">Register only. The RP advertises exactly these algorithms, in this order of preference, instead of its default list.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="field">
                    <label class="checkbox">
                        <input type="checkbox" id="option-excludecredentials" checked>
                        Exclude existing credentials
                    </label>
                    <p class="help">Register only. When on (the WebAuthn default) the RP lists the user's existing credentials in excludeCredentials, so an authenticator that already holds one refuses to create another. Turn off to register several credentials (for example PQC and classical) on the same key for comparison.</p>
                </div>
            </form>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>